WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.730
"Bergamo Alta"

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:06.160
Amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:21.210
I want to protect you and fulfill
my promise to the only one for me

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:28.680
In a world filled with doubt,
I still can't find the answer

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:35.760
Even so, I continue forward... Why?

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:46.200
If I can change this dream-like
reality with my own two hands,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:53.710
amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:01:53.710 --> 00:02:01.380
I want to protect the only one for me

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:09.220
I swear on my beating heart I will
continue to run until I burn away

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:16.730
Amid the eternal love
I feel simply by living,

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:24.760
I want to fulfill my promise

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.840
"Frascati"

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.900
Caterina-ojousama!

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.660
Domenico! Paola! It's been a while!

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.970
How many years has it been?
I was so surprised when you called!

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.040
Sorry for being so sudden.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.050
My friends and I need
to stay here for a while.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.140
Certainly, certainly! Please
make yourselves at home!

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:20.530
Franco-sama. Thank you
for always looking after her!

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.070
No, she's the one who looks after me.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:28.770
This is Pinocchio. He'll be
working with us for a while.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.030
It's nice to meet you.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:38.310
- Where is this?
- Franca's vineyard.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.870
That married couple is
in charge of running it.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.220
The white wine here is delicious.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:47.050
I don't drink wine.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:54.500
It was likely the Social Welfare
Agency you ran into in Montalcino.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.870
They're hindering our activities
all around the country.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:01.640
We're at the farm in Frascati.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.640
We're going to plan out
the bridge bombing here.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:09.210
Understood. If anything
happens, call the usual number.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:12.240
Umm, do you want to talk to Pinocchio?

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.520
No, that'll be all right.
I leave him in your hands.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.690
Say, Cristiano.
The pendant Pinocchio wore...

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.360
Was it important?

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:27.500
I gave it to him a long time ago.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.330
Oh.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.370
We have a plan
underway in Rome to kidnap

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:36.970
the chairwoman of the Messina
Bridge Development Corporation.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:40.210
Its success or failure will
likely change any future plans.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.840
Yes. I would think so.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.310
It's being led by
Nino Ferretti, from Bergamo.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.880
I believe you two have met before?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.780
Nino?

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:56.220
"Retirement of the Tibetan Terrier"

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.650
"Chairwoman's Home"

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.440
Here it comes. The chairwoman's car.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:12.270
No escort cars today, either...

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:17.410
She's as naive as always.
Tell Cosimo and Corra to tail her.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.110
Leone.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.050
According to Sergio,

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:24.590
her security is being replaced soon.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.020
Remain cautious until
we know who they are.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:31.490
Come on, Nino. Don't you think
we're being a little too passive?

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:35.550
Acting cautiously is how I do things.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:10.130
That's the end.

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.030
Thank you, young lady.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.870
That was a very nice performance.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:26.410
Well? She seems just like an
ordinary girl, wouldn't you say?

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:29.780
I'm shocked. She really
has a mechanical body?

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:34.190
We use medical reconstruction
techniques to recreate lifelike flesh:

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:38.990
Skin and bones made of new materials,
as well as artificial muscle.

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:41.330
They're not exactly "superhuman,"

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.870
but they're several times stronger
and quicker than the average person

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:47.200
and obey orders.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:50.370
Still, using children like this...

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:54.510
The younger the patient, the more
adaptable the brain is to the body.

00:06:54.510 --> 00:07:00.210
Isabella, in almost all cases,
national security is given top priority.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:03.850
That's how society's
peace of mind is maintained.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:07.790
I don't come from a public
safety background like you.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:10.390
This is hard for me to accept...

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:11.760
Chairwoman.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:14.760
You do realize our nation's
medical reconstruction techniques

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:18.030
are the most advanced
in the world, correct?

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:23.570
This is because our cybernetic
research also benefits society.

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:26.810
We currently provide hundreds
of patients around the country

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:29.540
with artificial limbs at no cost,

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:34.950
and I'm sure it won't be too long
until we can treat your legs, too.

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:38.720
I do sympathize with the children,

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:43.260
but there are many more who
can be saved because of them.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.830
Our background checks of
everyone close to the chairwoman

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:48.160
will be complete in a few days.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.630
According to the Padania
agent we caught the other day,

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:53.430
the countdown for the
kidnapping has begun.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.070
Hurry things up as much as possible.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.130
Understood.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.140
Giuse-san!

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.610
Henrietta. That was a wonderful
performance. You've improved!

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:08.050
Thank you!

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:29.800
What is that, Henrietta?

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:34.880
A kaleidoscope.
Giuse-san got it for me in France.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.940
Is it like a gun scope?

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:39.170
Here, have a look!

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:44.180
And then you turn this wheel.

00:08:45.890 --> 00:08:47.510
It's pretty...

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.000
Rico, how could you?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.070
I-I'm sorry, Henrietta.

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:05.040
Why did you turn it so hard?!

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:15.870
Did you say something
mean to Rico, Henrietta?

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.760
She didn't mean it,
so you need to forgive her.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:26.130
I'm the one to blame.
That lousy antique shop owner...

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:29.330
No! It's not your fault at all!

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:31.400
I'll let a skilled repairman see it,

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:34.890
so you need to make up
with Rico when it's fixed.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:39.230
Come on, now. Show me a smile!

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:42.570
Yes, sir...

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:53.580
Ludovico here. Still no change
at the chairwoman's estate.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:57.160
Welcome!

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:00.860
I was told you repair antiques here...

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:04.590
We fix most anything.
Let me see what you have.

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:11.410
Oh, this is an unusual kaleidoscope.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.710
I have my hands full at the moment,
so it might take some time.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:15.780
Is that all right?

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:18.440
I guess we have no choice.

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:26.120
No, I've changed my mind.
I'll have it done in three days.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:32.230
Hired hands like me need something
that makes the job worthwhile.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:36.290
I can't let the little
girl grow even sadder.

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:42.300
A teary-eyed girl showed up with
this kaleidoscope one afternoon.

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:45.670
She had a slight scent of pine resin.

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:51.130
Pine resin... Probably the
kind used on violin bows.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:55.380
Don't you just sense
some sort of drama in it?

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:58.650
It's jobs like that that I love.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:06.760
How does the security issue look, Alfonso?

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:10.030
There's no problem with
the bulletproof exterior.

00:11:10.030 --> 00:11:12.870
We'll just need to leave
a fire extinguisher inside,

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.470
and turn off the driver's-side airbag.

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:16.770
I see.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:19.940
What's the matter? Is something wrong?

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:24.050
Kaschmann-san. Why does she not
bring escorts when going places?

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:27.820
She isn't fond of excessive security.

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:32.490
How carefree. Especially when her
husband died in a terrorist attack.

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:35.960
Is there any way I can help you?

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:40.290
No, thank you. We will handle
everything from here on out.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.560
Please have the mansion's
security staff go on vacation.

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:13.720
Thanks, Henrietta...

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.910
It's almost as if a war
is about to start...

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:29.110
The Five Republics Faction is
out to get you, D'Angelo-san.

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:31.550
This is for your own safety.

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.650
Yes, I know.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:37.690
You can always look away if you'd
rather not see any unpleasantness.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:40.750
But this is what we do.

00:12:41.790 --> 00:12:44.090
Yes... I apologize...

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.930
I made him angry.

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:52.400
- Come again?
- Croce-san...

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:58.310
I found out just now, but misfortune
befell his own family long ago...

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:00.210
He's frightening...

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:03.380
It's almost like I can see
the color of hatred inside him...

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.510
Giuse-san is a nice person!

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:08.080
Even yesterday, even though
he was busy with work,

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:10.480
he took me with him
to have my kaleidoscope fixed!

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:14.780
There's no one in all
of Italy as nice as him!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:19.760
Oh... I'm sorry, then...

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:24.900
In that case, his hatred must
have quietly changed him...

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:29.240
Do you not hate terrorists, D'Angelo-san?

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:33.670
Oh, I did, a long time ago.
What about you?

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:37.780
It's not so much hate as there
is a reason to kill them...

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:41.450
And if that's what Giuse-san wants, then...

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:46.050
I've lost my certainty...

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:50.090
I wanted to fulfill my late
husband's wish and finish the bridge,

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:55.150
but I don't know if it is worth
shedding so much blood over...

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:02.440
Nino, have you fixed
the kaleidoscope already?

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:05.940
Yes. The spindle broke off,
so I made a new one.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:09.680
Oh? That's pretty slick.
Where'd you learn to do that?

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:13.210
I used to tinker with these
kinds of things a long time ago.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:15.950
Take a look at this. It's interesting.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.090
Whoa, what's this? Balzac?

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:22.290
"Lily of the Valley," 1836.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.890
It's a worthless phony, but it's nicely done.

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:25.860
Yes.

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:28.000
Does the client know?

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.830
I'm sure he's aware.

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:33.990
He did seem like someone
who can appreciate a good joke.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:39.140
With things like this, it's the
thought that matters the most.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:01.550
Franca...

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:08.270
I've been hearing about your exploits.

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:10.840
- Ls Franco doing well?
- Yes.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:14.940
I thought he'd never be
able to handle women...

00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:16.910
Guess I was wrong.

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:22.020
I heard from Cristiano...

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:25.190
Have you really given up bomb-making?

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:26.520
Yeah.

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:30.020
There's something I'd like you
to help with. With your help...

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:32.090
The Messina Bridge, right?

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:36.960
To blow up something that big,
you need an equal amount of passion.

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:38.700
Like you.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:41.340
But don't you want
to avenge your brother?

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:46.110
Do you know what my
associates call me now?

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:49.770
A Tibetan Terrier that can no longer run.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:54.820
I'll be in Rome for a few days.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.940
Call if you change your mind.

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:17.140
What is it, Nino?

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.970
Who's this girl?

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:22.080
According to Sergio,
she's a relative of the chairwoman.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.910
She's in Rome on vacation.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.640
Oh...

00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.980
Yeah?

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:33.350
Nino.

00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:36.790
The authorities have caught our
associate in the magazine company.

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:40.390
I see. Then it's only a matter of time

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.030
until they learn about this kidnapping.

00:16:42.030 --> 00:16:46.100
What now? Should we
make our move tomorrow?

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.570
- The plan is off.
- What?!

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:53.240
I recognized the older man
who got out of the car just now.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:56.940
A sharp man who was once part of a
Ministry of Interior anti-terrorism unit.

00:16:56.940 --> 00:16:59.000
The risk is too great.

00:16:59.850 --> 00:17:04.840
We're ceasing our surveillance
and leaving. Gather all the others.

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:20.200
Damn! We should've just
made our move sooner!

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:24.410
Why did Milan choose Nino instead of you?!

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:27.840
Because he hates
bloodshed and acts cautiously.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:31.810
Leone, you and Nino
go way back, don't you?

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:38.050
I first met him when he was still
just a student at Turin Polytechnic.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:47.230
He and his brother crafted bombs
and blew things up at random.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:49.330
He was a real reliable friend.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:51.570
Nino was?

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:55.870
But after the police killed his brother,
he suddenly turned timid.

00:17:55.870 --> 00:18:00.340
His friends even referred to
him as the "Tibetan Terrier."

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:02.110
Tibetan Terrier?

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:04.780
An ornamental dog from Tibet.

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:07.250
Alert and agile, but docile.

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:11.220
Hey, Leone. What do you
say we kill her ourselves?

00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:13.990
I was considering that myself.

00:18:13.990 --> 00:18:16.220
We have no need for cowards.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.070
What happened, Kaschmann-san?

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:28.800
Weren't you going on vacation?

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:31.670
There's nothing else for me to do, actually.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:37.280
I have been in charge of her security
for five years straight now...

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:40.580
Who might that little girl be?

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:43.780
She's one of the chairwoman's
relatives from Padua.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:46.050
That's strange.

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:49.390
I've never once heard about her.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:52.360
Why does it matter to you...

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:55.590
Hugon Kaschmann, a.k.a. Sergio Aimaro?!

00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:59.500
We ran checks on everyone
close to the chairwoman

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.140
before we even came here.

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:04.300
After tapping phones,
inspecting bank accounts,

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:06.810
and scouring all public records,

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:09.810
we learned that you're
actually a Padania agent

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:12.970
who's changed his
name and his face twice!

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:22.860
That saved us the
trouble of looking for him.

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:26.660
Ferro, we'll use him
for the decoy operation.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.150
Understood.

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:46.580
According to Sergio,

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:50.750
the chairwoman's car will arrive
at the church in 10 minutes.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:55.690
She can't use her legs, so she'll be
vulnerable as she's exiting the car.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:59.350
Kill the escorts and kidnap
the chairwoman and the girl.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:33.220
Damn!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.230
Alright! Go!

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:11.300
Rico, never use two shots at this distance.

00:21:11.300 --> 00:21:14.760
Yes. I'm sorry, Jean-san.

00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:47.930
"Termini Station"

00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:51.100
I can't go on any longer as an activist.

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:55.540
After my brother died, the question
would never leave my head.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:59.850
The question of whether or not
what we do is worth killing for...

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:01.320
Nino...

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:05.790
There was a time when I wouldn't
have given it a second thought.

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:07.290
I don't like this.

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:10.520
Yeah, I bet. But you'll understand someday.

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:12.630
How can you be so sure?

00:22:12.630 --> 00:22:16.330
Franca, what is it you're fighting against?

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:18.730
When will victory be yours?

00:22:19.370 --> 00:22:22.070
To avenge your old man...

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:25.840
...who will you have to kill first?

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:29.040
Think that over now, while you can.

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:34.500
Before you turn into an old dog,
like me, that can't run anymore.

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:42.060
What do you think? It's all fixed up!
Maybe even better than before!

00:22:42.060 --> 00:22:43.420
Little lady.

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:45.830
Be sure to oil it once in a while, okay?

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:47.350
Okay!

00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:52.200
Umm, is the employee
who fixed it not here today?

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:53.630
I'd like to thank him...

00:22:53.630 --> 00:22:57.540
Oh. Ol' Nino suddenly quit.

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:00.370
He was such a skilled
and hard worker, too...

00:23:45.190 --> 00:24:00.030
A doll without a heart,
born from warm hands

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:09.510
I neither smile nor talk

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:17.780
I want you to hear about
these feelings someday,

00:24:17.780 --> 00:24:25.730
though they can't be put into words

00:24:25.730 --> 00:24:34.000
I'll summon all my strength

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:45.940
to know what it means to live

00:25:01.520 --> 00:25:06.550
"Caterina and the Circle of Revenge"
